signet-nip46-client
===================

This crate was moved from the `decented-signet` crate
(forgesworn/signet-play, revision 55723d3a320150f90bac34fc2a7615fb69e11606,
src/nip46.rs), together with its unit tests, by the same author. The code
changed only where it had to stand alone: the relay types now come from the
`fray-relay-client` crate, two items were made public (`generate_connect_secret`
and `RemoteSigner::request_with_id`), the module's provenance paragraph was
rewritten, the two widened items got new doc comments (`request_with_id`'s
one-line comment was replaced), and the tests name "Example App" in place of a
game. It is
distributed under the MIT License; see LICENSE.

Before that, the code was ported from the vendored NIP-46 client of an earlier
game codebase by the same author, at source commit
bdd4fe877acf3a6f4ca3174d1ce79c6672935e2f: the URI builder, the one-shot connect
secret, the constant-time echo check, the secret-less persisted session and the
tests were kept. The rust-nostr `NostrConnect` transport was replaced by a
request loop on signet-play's relay trait (now the `Relay` trait of
`fray-relay-client`), and `perms` was added to the `nostrconnect://` URI.

That vendored client was a mirror of signet-nip46-client 0.1, which is kept in
forgesworn/signet-nip46-client-legacy (private) (canonical commit
5b85902f4655e541d4c631da5bc3257868dcc96a, plus the earlier codebase's
nostrconnect-secret divergence). This crate replaces that one under the same
name; it shares no history with it.

